/*!
\page page_stPhmdDetector StPhmdDetector

\brief One detector plane (PMD or CPV) of the STAR Photon Multiplicity Detector.

\section phmdDetector_overview Overview

StPhmdDetector represents one complete plane of the STAR PHMD (2.3 < η < 3.9):
the PMD photon-detection plane (kPmdId, behind lead converter) or the CPV
charged-particle veto plane (kPhmdCpvId, in front of lead).  It owns the
array of 12 StPhmdModule supermodule objects, per-supermodule hit counts, and
the StPhmdClusterCollection produced during reconstruction.

\section phmdDetector_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StPhmdDetector
\endcode

Managed by \ref page_stPhmdCollection "StPhmdCollection".

\section phmdDetector_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| StDetectorId | mDetectorId | kPmdId or kPhmdCpvId. |
| Int_t[12] | mModulesNHit | Hit count per supermodule. |
| StPhmdModule*[12] | mModules | Owned supermodule array. |
| StPhmdClusterCollection* | mClusters | Owned cluster collection. |

\section phmdDetector_methods Key Methods

- \c id() — detector identifier.
- \c numberOfModules() — returns 12.
- \c addHit(StPhmdHit*) — route a hit to the correct supermodule.
- \c moduleHits(uint) — hit count for one supermodule.
- \c module(uint) — access a supermodule.
- \c cluster() — cluster collection.
- \c setCluster(), \c setModule() — setters.

\section phmdDetector_seealso See Also

\ref page_stPhmdHit "StPhmdHit",
\ref page_stPhmdModule "StPhmdModule",
\ref page_stPhmdCluster "StPhmdCluster"
*/
